<gpx version="1.1" creator="Trail Analytics" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><wpt lat="40.15964" lon="-105.48727"><name>Hairpin #1 (rocky)</name><desc>P1; unverified; 105-degree hairpin (geometry-detected). 4x4explore: rocky sections concentrate at the hairpins. Description-to-location mapping approximate.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.14587" lon="-105.48607"><name>Hairpin #2 (rocky, pick your line)</name><desc>P1; designated; 119-degree hairpin at mile ~2.65 (geometry-detected), coincides with the steep zone's south end.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.14387" lon="-105.48904"><name>Steepest sustained pitch (21% max grade, mile ~3.1)</name><desc>P1; designated; DEM-derived: steepest zone on the route. Obstacle candidate — top capture priority. Interesting: matches 4x4explore's 'rocky sections ~2/3 through' better than the hairpins do.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.13456" lon="-105.50819"><name>Descent switchback (upper)</name><desc>P1; designated; 138-degree turn starting the final descent to Peaceful Valley.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.13439" lon="-105.50279"><name>Descent switchback (lower) — roughest section</name><desc>P1; unverified; 142-degree turn. 4x4explore: second hairpin 'much rougher', larger rocks, pick your line, just before crossing back near private property.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.144752879115075" lon="-105.48636474028177"><name>Sustained grade · mile 2.94</name><desc>P2; designated; DEM candidate: inspect the road alignment and terrain before choosing a capture location.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.16835887876956" lon="-105.47550845734249"><name>Grade variation · mile 0.60</name><desc>P3; designated; DEM candidate: inspect the road alignment and terrain before choosing a capture location.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.159876687787765" lon="-105.48504053944775"><name>Grade variation · mile 1.39</name><desc>P3; designated; DEM candidate: inspect the road alignment and terrain before choosing a capture location.</desc></wpt><wpt lat="40.15530977620244" lon="-105.4847